", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-1676082\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-1676082.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10935673, \"displayName\": \"PTEN dephosphorylates PIP3\", \"followingEvent\": [10959275], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PTEN dephosphorylates PIP3\", \"PI(3,4,5)P3 is dephosphorylated to PI (4,5)P2 by PTEN at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-199456\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-199456.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10959120, \"displayName\": \"PI5P is phosphorylated to PI(4,5)P2 by PIP4K2 dimers at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [10959275], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI5P is phosphorylated to PI(4,5)P2 by PIP4K2 dimers at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-1675776\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-1675776.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"CEL\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 68320, \"displayName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"name\": [\"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"C.elegans\", \"C. elegans\", \"Ce\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"6239\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-1676048\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-1676048.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9990864, \"displayName\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\"}]}"
