ecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-426639\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-426639.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 2046047, \"displayName\": \"THA-CoA [peroxisomal matrix]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"THA-CoA\", \"(6Z,9Z,12Z,15Z,18Z,21Z)-tetracosahexaenoyl-CoA\", \"6Z,9Z,12Z,15Z,18Z,21Z-tetracosahexaenoyl-CoA (THA-CoA)\", \"6,9,12,15,18,21-24:6(n-3)\"], \"producedByEvent\": [10962889], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-2046047\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-2046047.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"CEL\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 68320, \"displayName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"name\": [\"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"C.elegans\", \"C. elegans\", \"Ce\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"6239\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-2046087\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-2046087.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9990864, \"displayName\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\"}]}"
      }
